<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="032" project="spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI">
  <metadata>
    <title>Flip dev to MI-FIC via slot swap, then soak (FR-C2)</title>
    <phase>3 Rollout</phase>
    <gate>031 fully green</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>auth tag, live environment change with total-outage blast radius.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Prescriptive operational sequence; the judgment was made in 031.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Live flip on the only running environment.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>031</deps>
    <tags>auth,deploy,rollout</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours plus soak</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Swap the verified slot into production on dev so MI-FIC becomes the live credential, then soak before anything is removed. The secret remains configured as the fallback throughout.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer executing a controlled production flip.</role>
  <goal>Dev running on MI-FIC, with the §6.1 checklist re-passed post-swap and a soak period elapsed with no auth errors.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>#3b attempt 1 took dev down with a SIGABRT from an eager connect under ValidateOnBuild. That is why the rule is: no in-session flips, slot swap only. Rollback is swapping back, or reordering credentials — both config-level.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/decisions/031-obo-verification-dev.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="031" status="pending">Fully green verification checklist</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: swap ONLY. Do not remove the secret, do not touch Key Vault, do not edit scripts — all of that is 033, after the soak.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: SITE PROPERTIES DO NOT SWAP -- only app settings and code do. keyVaultReferenceIdentity, and the slot's managed-identity assignment, must already be correct on BOTH slots before the swap; they will not arrive via it. Verify both sides first. See notes/decisions/001-slot-creation.md Finding A.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: do NOT use Deploy-BffApi.ps1 -UseSlotDeploy as the swap mechanism -- it re-deploys first. This task swaps an ALREADY-VERIFIED slot. Use az webapp deployment slot swap directly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: NO in-session flips. Swap as a discrete, announced operation with the rollback command prepared in advance.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: if anything looks wrong post-swap, swap BACK first and diagnose afterwards. Do not fix forward on a fail-closed auth path.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>App Service slot swap, staged auth rollout</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step>Confirm 031 is fully green and its record is committed.</step>
    <step>Prepare and rehearse the rollback command (swap back) before swapping.</step>
    <step>Swap the slot into production.</step>
    <step>Immediately re-run the §6.1 checklist against the production slot.</step>
    <step>Monitor for the agreed soak period; watch auth failure rates and AuditEnrichmentMiddleware output.</step>
    <step>Record the swap time, soak window and observations.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Any post-swap checklist item fails — SWAP BACK IMMEDIATELY, then diagnose. Do not deliberate while users are locked out.</trigger>
    <trigger>Auth error rates rise during the soak — swap back and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI/notes/decisions/032-dev-flip-record.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Pre-swap: keyVaultReferenceIdentity and the managed-identity assignment are verified correct on BOTH slots, since site properties do not swap.</criterion>
    <criterion>Dev runs on MI-FIC as the first-priority credential.</criterion>
    <criterion>The full §6.1 checklist passes post-swap.</criterion>
    <criterion>The soak period elapsed with no auth-related errors.</criterion>
    <criterion>The secret is STILL configured and still selectable as fallback.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: the rollback path was rehearsed and is demonstrably available (swap back tested or verified).</criterion>
    <criterion>Swap time and soak window are recorded.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
